Package: rngat
Title: Stateless Random Numbers via Counter-Based Generation
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Pedro", "Baltazar", , "pedrobtz@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("D. E. Shaw Research", role = "cph",
           comment = "Random123 library, src/Random123/"),
    person("NumPy Developers", role = "cph",
           comment = "Ziggurat constant tables, src/numpyzig/")
  )
Description: Stateless deterministic random number generation using the Philox
    counter-based generator from the 'Random123' library by Salmon, Moraes,
    Dror and Shaw (2011) <doi:10.1145/2063384.2063405>. Random values are pure
    functions of immutable keys and sampler arguments, so sampling never reads
    or mutates '.Random.seed'. Independent substreams are requested as key
    vectors with rng_key(seed, n) or derived explicitly with rng_fold().
